author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "The output-budget corpus is measured against a workspace whose per-item collection depth is representative, not only its item count, and the corpus includes comments-audit, notes on a note-heavy item, assurance run, and bare list; A declared ceiling is enforced at runtime by default so a command degrades deterministically rather than exceeding its own contract; The gate's corpus adequacy is itself asserted, so a corpus that cannot trigger any known overrun fails the gate; The ten measured overruns are each either brought under their declared ceiling or have their ceiling re-declared with recorded rationale; list-closed and the other status aliases carry a declared ceiling"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: high
confidence: 95
resolution: Implemented representative corpus coverage and default runtime enforcement.
expected_result: Representative deep corpus deterministically enforces declared ceilings.
actual_result: "Thirty-two surfaces, including deep comments/notes/assurance, bind defaults and pass the negative control."
